note       rp: greedy 128 ids Qwen3-8B, spark1 original
 A hash table is a data structure that maps keys to values using a hash function. When two different keys produce the same hash value, a collision occurs. There are several methods to handle collisions in a hash table:

1. **Separate Chaining**: Each bucket in the hash table contains a linked list (or another data structure) of entries that have the same hash value. When a collision occurs, the new entry is added to the linked list. This method is efficient and can handle a large number of collisions.

